Subject: [PATCH] lib: omit the shared-library launcher interpreter in bundled builds

libfrr's optional executable-library version helper embeds an .interp
section. Archiving that same object into libfrr.a carries PT_INTERP into
fully static daemons. musl then enters its dynamic loader with no dynamic
dependencies (and, for non-PIE, no dynamic table), crashing during startup.

These packages ship daemon executables, not a directly executed libfrr.so.
Omit the optional library launcher section. The compiler/linker still emits
the normal interpreter for genuinely dynamically linked executables.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [packaging: the executable-library launcher is not shipped]

--- a/lib/libfrr.c
+++ b/lib/libfrr.c
@@ -1455,10 +1455,6 @@
 	*statep = NULL;
 }
 
-#ifdef INTERP
-static const char interp[]
-	__attribute__((section(".interp"), used)) = INTERP;
-#endif
 /*
  * executable entry point for libfrr.so
  *
